---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumb } from '../lib/page-schema';

const place = `${SITE.address.city}, ${SITE.address.region} ${SITE.address.zip}`;
const host = new URL(SITE.origin).hostname.replace(/^www\./, '');
const graph = [
  breadcrumb([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  schemaName={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses, and shares information from this website, by phone, and by text message.`}
  fullTitle
  extraGraph={graph}
>
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <article class="policy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-date">Effective date: October 24, 2026</p>
        <p>
          {SITE.name} ("we," "us," or "our") provides electrical service information and service requests for Sioux Falls,
          SD and nearby towns. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect through {host}, by phone, and by
          text message, how we use it, and the choices you have.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.name}<br />
          {place}<br />
          Phone: <a class="text-link" href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>
        </p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Information you give us. When you send a service request through our website, we collect the details you enter,
          such as your name, phone number, email address if you provide it, town, the service you need, company name if
          you provide it, and a description of the problem, along with the page of our website you sent it from. If you
          contact us another way, we receive whatever information you choose to share, such as your email address and the
          contents of your message.
        </p>
        <p>
          Call and text data. When you call or text us, our phone service provider records information such as your phone
          number, the date, time, and length of the call, the content of text messages, and any voicemail you leave.
        </p>
        <p>
          Technical information. Like most websites, our site and its hosting providers may automatically log basic
          technical information such as your IP address, browser type, and the pages you visit.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul class="job-list">
          <li>To respond to your service request and answer your questions.</li>
          <li>To contact you by phone or text message about your request.</li>
          <li>To schedule appointments and follow up on service.</li>
          <li>To keep our website working and secure.</li>
          <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How your service request is fulfilled</h2>
        <p>
          When you request service, we may pass your request, including your name, phone number, town, and problem
          description, to an independent local electrical service provider so they can contact you and complete the work.
          That provider uses your information only to respond to and fulfill your request. We do not sell your personal
          information.
        </p>

        <h2>Text messaging</h2>
        <p>
          If you check the text message consent box on our form, you agree to receive text messages from {SITE.name} about
          your service request and appointments. Consent to receive text messages is optional and is not a condition of
          requesting service.
        </p>
        <ul class="job-list">
          <li>Message frequency varies.</li>
          <li>Msg and data rates may apply.</li>
          <li>Reply STOP at any time to opt out. You will receive one message confirming you have been unsubscribed.</li>
          <li>
            Reply HELP for help, or call us at <a class="text-link" href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="policy-callout">
          No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Text
          messaging originator opt-in data and consent will not be shared with any third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>How we share information</h2>
        <p>We share information only as follows:</p>
        <ul class="job-list">
          <li>With a local electrical service provider to fulfill your request, as described above.</li>
          <li>
            With companies that help us run our website, forms, and phone and text messaging service, only as needed to
            provide those services.
          </li>
          <li>When required by law, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of our customers, the public, or us.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>All sharing is subject to the text messaging commitments in this policy.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
        <p>
          We keep your information for as long as needed to respond to your request and for our normal business records,
          and then delete it or keep it securely stored.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect information</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable safeguards to protect your information. No method of transmission or storage is completely
          secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>Our website is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you by calling <a class="text-link" href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>. You can stop text messages at any time by
          replying STOP.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will post the new version on this page with a
          new effective date.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions, call <a class="text-link" href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
